    <!-- About Content -->
    <div class="page-wrapper">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; font-weight:700; color:#1a237e; margin-bottom:14px;">About Railway Reservation System</h2>
        <p style="color:#444; font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:14px;">
            The Railway Reservation System is a comprehensive online platform that allows passengers to search for trains,
            check seat availability, and book tickets conveniently from anywhere. Our system aims to simplify the
            train-booking experience for millions of travellers across India.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#444; font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:14px;">
            A ticket, in either form, is required to obtain a boarding pass during check-in at the station.
            Then with the boarding pass and the attached ticket, the passenger is allowed to board the train.
            A train ticket is a document or electronic record, issued by the railway authority or a travel agency,
            that confirms that an individual is entitled to a seat on a scheduled train journey.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#444; font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:14px;">
            The ticket may be one of two types: a paper ticket, which comprises coupons or vouchers; and
            an electronic ticket (commonly referred to as an e-ticket). A ticket is generally only good for
            the train and journey date for which it was purchased. However, certain tickets allow flexible
            travel dates, sometimes on a standby basis or with a confirmed seat.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#444; font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:14px;">
            It is also possible to purchase an 'open' ticket, which allows travel on any train between the
            destinations listed on the ticket. The railway reservation system manages ticket issuance, seat
            allocation, passenger data, and revenue collection in an efficient and automated manner.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#444; font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.8;">
            Usually the ticket is for a specific journey. Some tickets are refundable. However, the lower cost
            tickets are usually not refundable and may carry many additional restrictions. The ticket, in either
            form, is required to board the train. Passengers are urged to carry their booking confirmation for
            verification purposes at any time during the journey.
        </p>
